    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by the high-efficiency matchup against Burrows. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** leads the charge with a 73.66 efficiency score, bolstered by a significant 17% boost from the opposing pitcher\u2019s skill profile and a 14% platoon advantage. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** (72.42) remains a near-elite start due to the favorable SP matchup and the added value derived from Burrows' slow delivery, which provides a tangible lift to **Jackson Merrill**\u2019s stolen base probability. **Andy Pages** (62.29) and **Curtis Mead** (62.15) round out our high-floor tier, with the former benefiting from a prime batting order position and the latter maximizing his dynamic platoon edge. While **Kyle Tucker** carries a lower projected output than his ceiling suggests due to a middling matchup against Freeland, his raw talent and favorable lineup slot keep him firmly in the \"Strong\" start category at 67.05.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved balancing the risk of the 34% rain probability for **Drake Baldwin** and **Dominic Smith** against the marginal upside of the rest of the bench. **Drake Baldwin** remains in the lineup despite a 59.21 score because his efficiency stays above our internal threshold, but he is a high-variance play given the potential for a shortened game. **Nasim Nunez** (58.63) occupies the final active slot; while his 9th-order position creates an efficiency drag, his versatility keeps him ahead of our deeper reserves. We are currently navigating a depleted roster with **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jorge Polanco** sidelined on the IL, leaving little room for error. The absence of **Gunnar Henderson** due to an off-day forces us to rely heavily on the **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**\u2013**Curtis Mead** middle-infield axis to carry our counting stats today. Keep a close eye on the weather in the games involving **Drake Baldwin** and **Dominic Smith**; if the rain risk intensifies, we will need to pivot to available non-rostered depth if the league rules permit, though currently, our bench options\u2014including **Josh Lowe**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Nolan Schanuel**, **Brayan Rocchio**, **Liam Hicks**, **Denzer Guzman**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Cole Carrigg**\u2014are either not in confirmed lineups or lack the matchup profile to displace our starters.",
